  "why": "Worn rectangular limestone in irregular courses, an edge course against the wall, a dished and rutted centre, kerbs and aprons at open edges, and shallow stepped ramps with landings and a central ramped strip wherever the lane is steeper than 1 in 8 (OldCityReferenceV2/reference-notes.md). Every dimension is drawn from a hash of the lane and the station, so no two stretches repeat."
